 "about": "What build/make_release.py trim_runtime() leaves of the runtime it downloads (standard I10 pins the download; this is taken from it after the digest is checked). library: the members of the runtime's own zip that stay. files: the files beside it that stay. Everything else goes. One list for both editions: the union of what they import. reviewed: each import a kept module could still try of a module that went, with the reason it does not run; build/runtime_check.py recomputes those from the bytecode at every build and stops on one that is not here, and on one here that no longer exists. A new Python's digest stops the build until python and sha256 here are changed; the same check then names every import of the new runtime that this list cuts and nobody has reviewed.",
